e it took so long that  he resigned his membership and the  complainant in that case labour activist  tweeted to say that she hopes kirsten  listens to her concerns and fixes this  broken system  labour is also not squeaky clean on this  are you no well a case like that is not  acceptable and i can tell you it  wouldn't happen again as well as being  the shadow business secretary i'm a  member of the labour party's national  executive committee i have the  humilities of it to know yes we have  problems i'm often a person who has to  respond and deal with those but i can  tell you that we don't have what i  observe in the conservative party which  is the repeated  decision to make the wrong decision if  that's in whatever short-term interest  they perceive they have i don't think  they've taken these things seriously i  think they've made decisions which they  shouldn't have made  i can't believe some of the things that  are in the papers today about what the  prime minister may have personally been  aware of before he made decisions like  this and but all the politics suffers  that there's no doubt about that it it  affects the reputation of us all that's  what i find so frustrating and i think  it's right that people demand better  you know it feels kind of slightly  depressing that you know i do these  interviews about these stories on a  regular relatively regular basis and i  often ask people what should actually  change in parliament and it feels as if  people just don't come up with any  answers teresa's coffee  was defending the use of bars defending  the use of mps directly employing their  staff i just wonder what your position  is on that 30 bars in the parliamentary  estate six in the house of commons the  house of lords is it now time to shut  the bars  look i don't think sophie parliament has  the kind of modern workplace culture  that it should have i think there's  further to go on that but i would just  say if you look at these particular  incidents 